     1	# Newton Development Guidelines
     2	
     3	- `newton/_src/` is internal. Examples and docs must not import from `newton._src`. Expose user-facing symbols via public modules (`newton/geometry.py`, `newton/solvers.py`, etc.).
     4	- Breaking changes require a deprecation first. Do not remove or rename public API symbols without deprecating them in a prior release.
     5	- Prefix-first naming for autocomplete: `ActuatorPD` (not `PDActuator`), `add_shape_sphere()` (not `add_sphere_shape()`).
     6	- Prefer nested classes for self-contained helper types/enums.
     7	- PEP 604 unions (`x | None`, not `Optional[x]`).
