     1	---
     2	name: newton-upstream-sync
     3	description: Safely sync a Newton research fork with `newton-physics/newton` when updating local or fork `main`, rebasing `research/pressure-field`, handling dirty worktrees, preserving old branch tips on backup branches, validating hydro-pressure behavior after a rebase, or cleaning up local branch and worktree state afterward.
     4	---
     5	
     6	# Newton Upstream Sync
     7	
     8	Keep `main` as a pure upstream integration branch. Keep pressure-field work on
     9	`research/pressure-field` or another dedicated research branch.
    10	
    11	## Clean Fast Path
    12	
    13	Use the bundled PowerShell workflow when the current checkout is clean:
    14	
    15	```powershell
    16	powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync_upstream.ps1
    17	```
    18	
    19	Useful variants:
    20	
    21	```powershell
    22	powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync_upstream.ps1 -CreateResearchBranch
    23	powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync_upstream.ps1 -Strategy merge
    24	powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync_upstream.ps1 -ResearchBranch research/my-experiment
    25	```
    26	
    27	The script refuses to run on a dirty worktree unless `-AllowDirty` is passed.
    28	Do not use `-AllowDirty` for branch surgery. Switch to the manual flow below.
    29	
    30	## Manual Flow For Dirty Worktrees
    31	
    32	If `git status --short --branch` is dirty, or the current checkout is on a
    33	research branch with uncommitted work, do not rewrite branches in place.
    34	
    35	1. Confirm remotes:
    36	
    37	```bash
    38	git remote -v
    39	```
    40	
    41	Expect `upstream` fetch to point at
    42	`https://github.com/newton-physics/newton.git`.
    43	
    44	2. Fetch upstream:
    45	
    46	```bash
    47	git fetch upstream
    48	```
    49	
    50	3. Preserve old fork tips on date-stamped backup branches before rewriting any
    51	remote branch:
    52	
    53	```bash
    54	git branch main-pre-upstream-sync-YYYYMMDD origin/main
    55	git push -u origin main-pre-upstream-sync-YYYYMMDD:main-pre-upstream-sync-YYYYMMDD
    56	
    57	git branch research/pressure-field-pre-upstream-rebase-YYYYMMDD research/pressure-field
    58	git push -u origin research/pressure-field-pre-upstream-rebase-YYYYMMDD:research/pressure-field-pre-upstream-rebase-YYYYMMDD
    59	```
    60	
    61	4. If the current checkout is dirty, update local `main` without checking it
    62	out there. First verify it is a pure fast-forward:
    63	
    64	```bash
    65	git rev-list --left-right --count main...upstream/main
    66	git merge-base --is-ancestor main upstream/main && echo fast-forward
    67	```
    68	
    69	If it is a clean fast-forward, move the ref directly:
    70	
    71	```bash
    72	git update-ref refs/heads/main refs/remotes/upstream/main <old-main-sha>
    73	```
    74	
    75	If it is not a fast-forward, stop and inspect the local `main` history before
    76	rewriting anything.
    77	
    78	5. Rewrite fork `main` only after preserving the old remote tip:
    79	
    80	```bash
    81	git push --force-with-lease=main:<old-origin-main-sha> origin main:main
    82	```
    83	
    84	## Rebase The Research Branch In A Clean Worktree
    85	
    86	Never run the rebase inside the dirty original checkout. Create a detached temp
    87	worktree from the research tip:
    88	
    89	```bash
    90	git worktree add --detach /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase research/pressure-field-pre-upstream-rebase-YYYYMMDD
    91	git -C /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase switch -c tmp/research-pressure-rebase-YYYYMMDD
    92	git -C /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase rebase main
    93	```
    94	
    95	If the rebase conflicts:
    96	
    97	- Inspect conflict markers directly in the temp worktree.
    98	- Compare the file on `main` with the final research branch state, not just the
    99	  first conflicting commit:
   100	
   101	```bash
   102	git show main:path/to/file
   103	git show research/pressure-field:path/to/file
   104	```
   105	
   106	- Prefer the final research-branch behavior when later pressure-field commits
   107	  already refactor the same code.
   108	- Continue with normal git commands:
   109	
   110	```bash
   111	git -C /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase add <resolved-files>
   112	GIT_EDITOR=true git -C /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase rebase --continue
   113	```
   114	
   115	## Verification
   116	
   117	For the pressure-field branch, run both a focused test slice and the example
   118	smoke test against the rebased tree.
   119	
   120	Prefer reusing the repo's existing `.venv` and point `PYTHONPATH` at the temp
   121	worktree instead of creating a fresh environment in `/tmp`:
   122	
   123	```bash
   124	MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp TMPDIR=/tmp PYTHONPATH=/tmp/newton-pressure-rebase \
   125	  /mnt/d/Biomotions/newton/.venv/bin/python -m newton.tests \
   126	  -p test_hydroelastic.py -k pressure --serial-fallback -q
   127	
   128	MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp TMPDIR=/tmp PYTHONPATH=/tmp/newton-pressure-rebase \
   129	  /mnt/d/Biomotions/newton/.venv/bin/python -m \
   130	  newton.examples.contacts.example_hydro_pressure_slice \
   131	  --test --viewer null --num-frames 1 --shape box
   132	```
   133	
   134	Notes:
   135	
   136	- The example is CUDA-only.
   137	- Inside restricted sandboxes, the unittest runner may need escalation so
   138	  `multiprocessing.Manager()` can bind locally.
   139	- Warp must see the real CUDA driver for meaningful pressure-field validation.
   140	
   141	## Publish The Rebases
   142	
   143	After verification succeeds:
   144	
   145	```bash
   146	git branch research/pressure-field-rebased-YYYYMMDD <rebased-sha>
   147	git push --force-with-lease=research/pressure-field:<old-origin-research-sha> \
   148	  origin tmp/research-pressure-rebase-YYYYMMDD:research/pressure-field
   149	```
   150	
   151	## Move The Original Checkout Onto The Clean Branch
   152	
   153	If the original checkout still contains branch-relative deletions or other
   154	local changes, stash them before switching:
   155	
   156	```bash
   157	git stash push -m 'pre-switch dirty deletions before moving to rebased pressure branch YYYY-MM-DD'
   158	```
   159	
   160	Then:
   161	
   162	```bash
   163	git branch -m research/pressure-field research/pressure-field-local-pre-rebase-YYYYMMDD
   164	git branch -m research/pressure-field-rebased-YYYYMMDD research/pressure-field
   165	git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/research/pressure-field research/pressure-field
   166	```
   167	
   168	Leave the stash in place unless you intentionally want to reapply those old
   169	changes.
   170	
   171	## Cleanup
   172	
   173	After the original checkout is on the clean rebased branch:
   174	
   175	```bash
   176	git branch -d tmp/research-pressure-rebase-YYYYMMDD
   177	git worktree remove /tmp/newton-pressure-rebase
   178	git worktree prune
   179	```
   180	
   181	If a temp worktree is broken and `git worktree remove` fails because its `.git`
   182	file points at stale metadata, remove both the temp directory and the matching
   183	`.git/worktrees/<name>` entry together.
   184	
   185	You can optionally retarget local backup branches so their upstream tracking
   186	matches the preserved backup remotes.

